{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1260769-limits-to-the-wizened-blessing","id":1260769,"title":"Limits to the Wizened Blessing","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-15T16:41:10-07:00","id":1260769,"title":"Limits to the Wizened Blessing","content":"Just what limits are there to this Blessing? Can it only apply to unworked materials, or can a sword be turned to diamond just as well as raw steel can? And what if instead of diamond, I wanted a sword of flame?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/665-shkspr1048","name":"shkspr1048","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"630"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T16:59:41-07:00","id":1260775,"title":"","content":"The limits to the blessing is that you need to be using either tools that you would normally use to work the material you're working with, or something that is analogous to it if you want to be risky. For example, if you were working with wood you'd need chisels and hammers, a handsaw or a jigsaw, and in turn you could make it into something else. If you were doing an existing sword, you could, but it would effectively be reforging a broken weapon into a new one.<br /> <br /> However, if you were to make a normally steel sword into flame, you'd have just that - flames. No mention is made of any equipment that a Wizened makes being anything other than mundane, even though they are explicitly using magic, and though I imagine that a Wizened can make items that can be made <i>into</i> supernatural equipment, they can't outright make it with their Blessing. To get a sword of fire that takes the shape of a sword and can be wielded as one, you'd need to branch into either Contracts for temporary weapons, or Tokens for permanent ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-15T17:00:49-07:00","id":1260776,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>shkspr1048</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1260769-limits-to-the-wizened-blessing#post1260769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just what limits are there to this Blessing? Can it only apply to unworked materials, or can a sword be turned to diamond just as well as raw steel can?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you can work a sword, you can work it into diamond. That's a real material with a shape that exists. You're rolling Wits + Crafts as an instant action with a -5 penalty or an extended action with at least six required successes, either one of which calls for an amount of invested time set by the ST; if you're improvising the tools then it can only be the former, it costs Glamour, and it has a higher risk of backfiring besides<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what if instead of diamond, I wanted a sword of flame? </div> </div> </div>What about it?<br /> <br /> The process being magical does not mean the result has any magical properties. A &quot;sword of flame&quot; that isn't just a metaphorical description of something else is a shape in a material that cannot hold a shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}